    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup heavily incentivized by stolen base upside and favorable platoon splits against mid-tier arms. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** stands as our highest-scoring asset at 80.98, buoyed by an elite 16% park factor and the opportunity to exploit the slow delivery of Trevor Rogers. Similarly, **Trea Turner** (75.29) and **Christian Yelich** (72.22) anchor the top of the order; both benefit from the optimal leadoff spot and favorable matchups against Brady Singer and Andre Pallante, respectively. **Yelich** specifically captures a massive 13% boost from his dynamic platoon split, while **Kyle Schwarber** (71.49) remains a high-floor play, carrying his xwOBA profile into a favorable matchup against the hittable Singer.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the final bench spots, where **Lars Nootbaar** (38.93) narrowly missed the cut. While **Nootbaar** offers a solid dynamic platoon advantage against Logan Henderson, his projected 8th-hole placement in the order acted as a drag on his utility, pushing him just below the threshold required to displace starters like **Luke Raley** or **Carson Benge**. We are monitoring the 33% rain risk in the games featuring **Caleb Durbin** and **Chase Meidroth**; should those contests face delays or cancellations, we have sufficient bench depth to pivot. The optimizer remains cautious of **Gary Sanchez**, whose 48.18 rating suggests he is a marginal start pending final lineup confirmation; if **Dillon Dingler** (38.79) finds his way into the lineup against Jack Perkins, we may need to re-evaluate our catching position to maximize our offensive efficiency.",
